{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MHR6eVe2pYRyentW5K5LY4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tsource_url: \"https://training.linuxfoundation.org/certification/kubernetes-cloud-native-associate/\"\n3\tfetched_at: \"2026-08-23T22:30:00-0400\"\n4\tauthority: \"The Linux Foundation / CNCF\"\n5\tobjectives_covered: [\"exam-format\", \"D1\", \"D2\", \"D3\", \"D4\"]\n6\tconcepts_covered: [\"kcna-exam-facts\", \"domain-weights\"]\n7\t---\n8\t# Kubernetes and Cloud Native Associate (KCNA) — Linux Foundation exam page\n9\t\n10\t\"The Kubernetes and Cloud Native Associate (KCNA) exam demonstrates a user's foundational knowledge and skills in Kubernetes and the wider cloud native ecosystem.\" Experience level: Beginner. Prerequisites: none.\n11\t\n12\t## Exam details\n13\t- Format: online, proctored, multiple-choice exam\n14\t- Duration: 90 minutes\n15\t- Pricing: exam only $250; exam + THRIVE-ONE annual subscription $495; exam + LFS250 course $299\n16\t- Included: 12-month eligibility window to schedule and take the exam; two exam attempts; certification valid for 2 years; exam preparation handbook\n17\t\n18\t## Domains & competencies\n19\t- Kubernetes Fundamentals — 44% (Kubernetes Core Concepts; Administration; Scheduling; Containerization)\n20\t- Container Orchestration — 28% (Networking; Security; Troubleshooting; Storage)\n21\t- Cloud Native Application Delivery — 16% (Application Delivery; Debugging)\n22\t- Cloud Native Architecture — 12% (Observability; Cloud Native Ecosystem and Principles; Cloud Native Community and Collaboration)\n23\t\n24\t## Not stated on this page\n25\tQuestion count and passing score are not published on the exam page. Third-party sources widely report 60 questions and a 75% passing score; treat those as commonly reported, not official.\n26\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6ba44a35-dfac-469b-9317-2d811c689d53","uuid":"3e442aac-2df4-48eb-a987-4b5ed40e21dc","timestamp":"2026-08-24T03:47:12.664Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\sources\\lf-kcna-exam-page-2026-08-23.md","content":"---\nsource_url: \"https://training.linuxfoundation.org/certification/kubernetes-cloud-native-associate/\"\nfetched_at: \"2026-08-23T22:30:00-0400\"\nauthority: \"The Linux Foundation / CNCF\"\nobjectives_covered: [\"exam-format\", \"D1\", \"D2\", \"D3\", \"D4\"]\nconcepts_covered: [\"kcna-exam-facts\", \"domain-weights\"]\n---\n# Kubernetes and Cloud Native Associate (KCNA) — Linux Foundation exam page\n\n\"The Kubernetes and Cloud Native Associate (KCNA) exam demonstrates a user's foundational knowledge and skills in Kubernetes and the wider cloud native ecosystem.\" Experience level: Beginner. Prerequisites: none.\n\n## Exam details\n- Format: online, proctored, multiple-choice exam\n- Duration: 90 minutes\n- Pricing: exam only $250; exam + THRIVE-ONE annual subscription $495; exam + LFS250 course $299\n- Included: 12-month eligibility window to schedule and take the exam; two exam attempts; certification valid for 2 years; exam preparation handbook\n\n## Domains & competencies\n- Kubernetes Fundamentals — 44% (Kubernetes Core Concepts; Administration; Scheduling; Containerization)\n- Container Orchestration — 28% (Networking; Security; Troubleshooting; Storage)\n- Cloud Native Application Delivery — 16% (Application Delivery; Debugging)\n- Cloud Native Architecture — 12% (Observability; Cloud Native Ecosystem and Principles; Cloud Native Community and Collaboration)\n\n## Not stated on this page\nQuestion count and passing score are not published on the exam page. Third-party sources widely report 60 questions and a 75% passing score; treat those as commonly reported, not official.\n","numLines":26,"startLine":1,"totalLines":26}}}
