{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011egUeG13zXaU8d4Qww4Ur9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tsource_url: \"https://training.linuxfoundation.org/kcna-program-changes/\"\n3\tfetched_at: \"2026-08-23T22:30:00-0400\"\n4\tauthority: \"The Linux Foundation / CNCF\"\n5\tobjectives_covered: [\"exam-format\", \"D4\"]\n6\tconcepts_covered: [\"curriculum-transition-2025-11-24\", \"observability-folded-into-architecture\"]\n7\t---\n8\t# KCNA Program Changes — Linux Foundation\n9\t\n10\t\"The Kubernetes and Cloud Native Associate (KCNA) exam will be updated no earlier than November 24, 2025.\"\n11\t\n12\tThe updated exam has four domains:\n13\t- Kubernetes Fundamentals – 44%: Kubernetes Core Concepts; Administration; Scheduling; Containerization\n14\t- Container Orchestration – 28%: Networking; Security; Troubleshooting; Storage\n15\t- Cloud Native Application Delivery – 16%: Application Delivery; Debugging\n16\t- Cloud Native Architecture – 12%: Observability; Cloud Native Ecosystem and Principles; Cloud Native Community and Collaboration\n17\t\n18\tWhat changed: observability is rolled under Cloud Native Architecture (it was previously a separate domain, \"Cloud Native Observability\", in the five-domain blueprint: Kubernetes Fundamentals 46%, Container Orchestration 22%, Cloud Native Architecture 16%, Cloud Native Observability 8%, Cloud Native Application Delivery 8%). The page does not specify question count, duration, or passing score.\n19\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6ba44a35-dfac-469b-9317-2d811c689d53","uuid":"463fbbdf-5d92-413d-97c3-825d0d20e2ee","timestamp":"2026-08-24T03:47:13.232Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\sources\\lf-kcna-program-changes-2026-08-23.md","content":"---\nsource_url: \"https://training.linuxfoundation.org/kcna-program-changes/\"\nfetched_at: \"2026-08-23T22:30:00-0400\"\nauthority: \"The Linux Foundation / CNCF\"\nobjectives_covered: [\"exam-format\", \"D4\"]\nconcepts_covered: [\"curriculum-transition-2025-11-24\", \"observability-folded-into-architecture\"]\n---\n# KCNA Program Changes — Linux Foundation\n\n\"The Kubernetes and Cloud Native Associate (KCNA) exam will be updated no earlier than November 24, 2025.\"\n\nThe updated exam has four domains:\n- Kubernetes Fundamentals – 44%: Kubernetes Core Concepts; Administration; Scheduling; Containerization\n- Container Orchestration – 28%: Networking; Security; Troubleshooting; Storage\n- Cloud Native Application Delivery – 16%: Application Delivery; Debugging\n- Cloud Native Architecture – 12%: Observability; Cloud Native Ecosystem and Principles; Cloud Native Community and Collaboration\n\nWhat changed: observability is rolled under Cloud Native Architecture (it was previously a separate domain, \"Cloud Native Observability\", in the five-domain blueprint: Kubernetes Fundamentals 46%, Container Orchestration 22%, Cloud Native Architecture 16%, Cloud Native Observability 8%, Cloud Native Application Delivery 8%). The page does not specify question count, duration, or passing score.\n","numLines":19,"startLine":1,"totalLines":19}}}
