{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01B99dPXNmEGJMchPiwLhbK9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tsource_url: \"https://training.linuxfoundation.org/certification-catalog/\"\n3\tfetched_at: \"2026-08-23T23:40:00-0400\"\n4\tauthority: \"The Linux Foundation certification catalog\"\n5\tobjectives_covered: [\"D4 Community and Collaboration\"]\n6\tconcepts_covered: [\"certification-ladder\", \"kcna\", \"kcsa\", \"cka\", \"ckad\", \"cks\", \"cnpa\", \"pca\", \"otca\", \"cgoa\", \"capa\", \"cca\"]\n7\t---\n8\t# Linux Foundation / CNCF cloud native certification catalog (training.linuxfoundation.org/certification-catalog/)\n9\t\n10\tBeginner (associate) level: KCNA — Kubernetes and Cloud Native Associate, foundational knowledge and skills in Kubernetes and the wider cloud native ecosystem; KCSA — Kubernetes and Cloud Native Security Associate; CNPA — Certified Cloud Native Platform Engineering Associate; CBA — Certified Backstage Associate; PCA — Prometheus Certified Associate; OTCA — OpenTelemetry Certified Associate; CGOA — Certified GitOps Associate; CAPA — Certified Argo Project Associate; CCA — Cilium Certified Associate; KCA — Kyverno Certified Associate.\n11\t\n12\tIntermediate (performance-based) level: CKA — Certified Kubernetes Administrator; CKAD — Certified Kubernetes Application Developer; CKS — Certified Kubernetes Security Specialist (requires an active CKA); CNPE — Certified Cloud Native Platform Engineer; ICA — Istio Certified Associate.\n13\t\n14\tThe associate exams are multiple choice; the CKA/CKAD/CKS exams are hands-on, performance-based exams in a live terminal.\n15\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6ba44a35-dfac-469b-9317-2d811c689d53","uuid":"4ad0916c-5af5-403f-b883-e98c476ec12f","timestamp":"2026-08-24T03:47:14.673Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\sources\\lf-cloud-native-certification-catalog-2026-08-23.md","content":"---\nsource_url: \"https://training.linuxfoundation.org/certification-catalog/\"\nfetched_at: \"2026-08-23T23:40:00-0400\"\nauthority: \"The Linux Foundation certification catalog\"\nobjectives_covered: [\"D4 Community and Collaboration\"]\nconcepts_covered: [\"certification-ladder\", \"kcna\", \"kcsa\", \"cka\", \"ckad\", \"cks\", \"cnpa\", \"pca\", \"otca\", \"cgoa\", \"capa\", \"cca\"]\n---\n# Linux Foundation / CNCF cloud native certification catalog (training.linuxfoundation.org/certification-catalog/)\n\nBeginner (associate) level: KCNA — Kubernetes and Cloud Native Associate, foundational knowledge and skills in Kubernetes and the wider cloud native ecosystem; KCSA — Kubernetes and Cloud Native Security Associate; CNPA — Certified Cloud Native Platform Engineering Associate; CBA — Certified Backstage Associate; PCA — Prometheus Certified Associate; OTCA — OpenTelemetry Certified Associate; CGOA — Certified GitOps Associate; CAPA — Certified Argo Project Associate; CCA — Cilium Certified Associate; KCA — Kyverno Certified Associate.\n\nIntermediate (performance-based) level: CKA — Certified Kubernetes Administrator; CKAD — Certified Kubernetes Application Developer; CKS — Certified Kubernetes Security Specialist (requires an active CKA); CNPE — Certified Cloud Native Platform Engineer; ICA — Istio Certified Associate.\n\nThe associate exams are multiple choice; the CKA/CKAD/CKS exams are hands-on, performance-based exams in a live terminal.\n","numLines":15,"startLine":1,"totalLines":15}}}
