{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UThDMUeZnrYA3KtGCZ4GvM","type":"tool_result","content":"# Linux Foundation Multiple Choice Exam FAQ - Key Extracts\n\n**(1) Number of Questions:**\nThe FAQ contains **no statement** about how many questions the exams contain, whether the number varies by exam, or any related information.\n\n**(2) Passing Score/Determination:**\n\"A score of 75% or above must be earned to pass the Multiple Choice Exam.\"\n\nThe FAQ does not mention scaled scoring, cut scores, or psychometric standard setting methods.\n\n**(3) Exam Duration:**\n\"Candidates are allowed 90 minutes to complete Multiple Choice Exams, with the exception of CNPA. CNPA candidates are allowed 120 minutes to complete the exam.\"\n\n**(4) Which Exams This FAQ Applies To:**\nThe FAQ titles itself \"Multiple Choice Exams: Frequently Asked Questions\" but **does not explicitly list which specific exams** it covers. CNPA is mentioned as an exception for timing. The renewal section references KCNA, KCSA, and CKA/CKAD/CKS in context of the CARE program, but doesn't state whether the entire FAQ applies to all these exams.\n\n**(5) Score/Cut Score Publication:**\nThe FAQ contains **no statement** about whether scores or cut scores are published publicly or made available to candidates beyond individual score reports."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6ba44a35-dfac-469b-9317-2d811c689d53","uuid":"1718dc75-25da-4c28-8b6f-50afa0c20901","timestamp":"2026-08-24T03:48:00.007Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":10418,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Linux Foundation Multiple Choice Exam FAQ - Key Extracts\n\n**(1) Number of Questions:**\nThe FAQ contains **no statement** about how many questions the exams contain, whether the number varies by exam, or any related information.\n\n**(2) Passing Score/Determination:**\n\"A score of 75% or above must be earned to pass the Multiple Choice Exam.\"\n\nThe FAQ does not mention scaled scoring, cut scores, or psychometric standard setting methods.\n\n**(3) Exam Duration:**\n\"Candidates are allowed 90 minutes to complete Multiple Choice Exams, with the exception of CNPA. CNPA candidates are allowed 120 minutes to complete the exam.\"\n\n**(4) Which Exams This FAQ Applies To:**\nThe FAQ titles itself \"Multiple Choice Exams: Frequently Asked Questions\" but **does not explicitly list which specific exams** it covers. CNPA is mentioned as an exception for timing. The renewal section references KCNA, KCSA, and CKA/CKAD/CKS in context of the CARE program, but doesn't state whether the entire FAQ applies to all these exams.\n\n**(5) Score/Cut Score Publication:**\nThe FAQ contains **no statement** about whether scores or cut scores are published publicly or made available to candidates beyond individual score reports.","durationMs":4199,"url":"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/faq-mc"}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YSt7NBPnqCKcEWyJ6YvU58","type":"tool_result","content":"# KCNA Certification - Extracted Information\n\n## Description and Target Audience\n\"The Kubernetes and Cloud Native Associate (KCNA) exam demonstrates a user's foundational knowledge and skills in Kubernetes and the wider cloud native ecosystem.\"\n\n\"The KCNA is a pre-professional certification designed for candidates interested in advancing to the professional level through a demonstrated understanding of kubernetes foundational knowledge and skills. This certification is ideal for students learning about or candidates interested in working with cloud native technologies.\"\n\n## Exam Specifications\n- **Format & Cost:** \"This exam is an online, proctored, multiple-choice exam.\" Cost is \"$250 and includes one free retake.\"\n- **Duration, Question Count, Passing Score:** Not specified in the provided content.\n- **Validity Period:** Not specified in the provided content.\n- **Prerequisites:** Not specified in the provided content.\n\n## Exam Domains and Weights\n| Domain | Weight |\n|--------|--------|\n| Kubernetes Fundamentals | 44% |\n| Container Orchestration | 28% |\n| Cloud Native Application Delivery | 16% |\n| Cloud Native Architecture | 12% |\n\n## Place Among CNCF Certifications\n\"The KCNA exam is intended to prepare candidates to work with cloud native technologies and pursue further CNCF credentials, including CKA, CKAD, and CKS.\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6ba44a35-dfac-469b-9317-2d811c689d53","uuid":"e2c9d7df-c762-465a-a39c-c915e5561003","timestamp":"2026-08-24T03:48:03.286Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":162829,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# KCNA Certification - Extracted Information\n\n## Description and Target Audience\n\"The Kubernetes and Cloud Native Associate (KCNA) exam demonstrates a user's foundational knowledge and skills in Kubernetes and the wider cloud native ecosystem.\"\n\n\"The KCNA is a pre-professional certification designed for candidates interested in advancing to the professional level through a demonstrated understanding of kubernetes foundational knowledge and skills. This certification is ideal for students learning about or candidates interested in working with cloud native technologies.\"\n\n## Exam Specifications\n- **Format & Cost:** \"This exam is an online, proctored, multiple-choice exam.\" Cost is \"$250 and includes one free retake.\"\n- **Duration, Question Count, Passing Score:** Not specified in the provided content.\n- **Validity Period:** Not specified in the provided content.\n- **Prerequisites:** Not specified in the provided content.\n\n## Exam Domains and Weights\n| Domain | Weight |\n|--------|--------|\n| Kubernetes Fundamentals | 44% |\n| Container Orchestration | 28% |\n| Cloud Native Application Delivery | 16% |\n| Cloud Native Architecture | 12% |\n\n## Place Among CNCF Certifications\n\"The KCNA exam is intended to prepare candidates to work with cloud native technologies and pursue further CNCF credentials, including CKA, CKAD, and CKS.\"","durationMs":5008,"url":"https://www.cncf.io/training/certification/kcna/"}}
