{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019QgLLezmogim7KUSTUpvQa","type":"tool_result","content":"# Linux Foundation Certification FAQ - Extracted Information\n\n**Number of Questions on Multiple-Choice Exams:**\nNot stated in the document.\n\n**Number of Questions on KCNA Exams:**\nNot stated in the document.\n\n**Passing Scores:**\n\"Please review the FAQ section of all our programs, to determine the score required to pass each exam.\" (The actual passing score percentages are not specified in this FAQ.)\n\n**Exam Duration:**\nNot stated in the document.\n\n**Retakes/Free Retake Policy:**\n\"There is no enforced wait period for retakes currently.\" Retakes are available if the first attempt received a \"No Pass\" grade, within 12 months of original purchase.\n\n**Certification Validity Period:**\nNot explicitly stated. The document mentions candidates can \"keep their certification current by retaking and passing the Certification Exam prior to the expiration of their certification,\" but the expiration timeframe is not specified here.\n\n**Eligibility Window:**\n\"Once you purchase an exam registration, you will have 12 months to take the exam.\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6ba44a35-dfac-469b-9317-2d811c689d53","uuid":"cf8f4dfe-8f33-452d-99d0-a7eb2e174e81","timestamp":"2026-08-24T03:48:24.099Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":22217,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Linux Foundation Certification FAQ - Extracted Information\n\n**Number of Questions on Multiple-Choice Exams:**\nNot stated in the document.\n\n**Number of Questions on KCNA Exams:**\nNot stated in the document.\n\n**Passing Scores:**\n\"Please review the FAQ section of all our programs, to determine the score required to pass each exam.\" (The actual passing score percentages are not specified in this FAQ.)\n\n**Exam Duration:**\nNot stated in the document.\n\n**Retakes/Free Retake Policy:**\n\"There is no enforced wait period for retakes currently.\" Retakes are available if the first attempt received a \"No Pass\" grade, within 12 months of original purchase.\n\n**Certification Validity Period:**\nNot explicitly stated. The document mentions candidates can \"keep their certification current by retaking and passing the Certification Exam prior to the expiration of their certification,\" but the expiration timeframe is not specified here.\n\n**Eligibility Window:**\n\"Once you purchase an exam registration, you will have 12 months to take the exam.\"","durationMs":3570,"url":"https://training.linuxfoundation.org/about/faqs/certification-faq/"}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XDbfhQks7f3tcFw3HGhPrc","type":"tool_result","content":"# KCNA Program Changes - Extracted Information\n\n**Effective Date:**\n\"no earlier than November 24, 2025\"\n\n**Announcement Wording:**\n\"The Kubernetes and Cloud Native Associate (KCNA) exam will be updated no earlier than November 24, 2025.\"\n\n**OLD Domain List with Weights:**\nThe page does NOT display the previous/retired domain structure or weights.\n\n**NEW Domain List with Weights and Competencies:**\n\n- **Kubernetes Fundamentals – 44%**\n  - Kubernetes Core Concepts\n  - Administration\n  - Scheduling\n  - Containerization\n\n- **Container Orchestration – 28%**\n  - Networking\n  - Security\n  - Troubleshooting\n  - Storage\n\n- **Cloud Native Application Delivery – 16%**\n  - Application Delivery\n  - Debugging\n\n- **Cloud Native Architecture – 12%**\n  - Observability\n  - Cloud Native Ecosystem and Principles\n  - Cloud Native Community and Collaboration\n\n**Key Change Statement:**\n\"The KCNA domains (i.e. Fundamentals, Container Orchestration etc.) will remain mostly unchanged except that observability will be rolled under Cloud Native Architecture.\"\n\n**Rationale:**\n\"These updates are part of our ongoing efforts to ensure that a Kubernetes and Cloud Native Associate (KCNA) has the most updated skills, knowledge, and competence needed in the industry.\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6ba44a35-dfac-469b-9317-2d811c689d53","uuid":"209e45c8-c50d-40a8-ad79-81c7b262979b","timestamp":"2026-08-24T03:48:28.210Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":7279,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# KCNA Program Changes - Extracted Information\n\n**Effective Date:**\n\"no earlier than November 24, 2025\"\n\n**Announcement Wording:**\n\"The Kubernetes and Cloud Native Associate (KCNA) exam will be updated no earlier than November 24, 2025.\"\n\n**OLD Domain List with Weights:**\nThe page does NOT display the previous/retired domain structure or weights.\n\n**NEW Domain List with Weights and Competencies:**\n\n- **Kubernetes Fundamentals – 44%**\n  - Kubernetes Core Concepts\n  - Administration\n  - Scheduling\n  - Containerization\n\n- **Container Orchestration – 28%**\n  - Networking\n  - Security\n  - Troubleshooting\n  - Storage\n\n- **Cloud Native Application Delivery – 16%**\n  - Application Delivery\n  - Debugging\n\n- **Cloud Native Architecture – 12%**\n  - Observability\n  - Cloud Native Ecosystem and Principles\n  - Cloud Native Community and Collaboration\n\n**Key Change Statement:**\n\"The KCNA domains (i.e. Fundamentals, Container Orchestration etc.) will remain mostly unchanged except that observability will be rolled under Cloud Native Architecture.\"\n\n**Rationale:**\n\"These updates are part of our ongoing efforts to ensure that a Kubernetes and Cloud Native Associate (KCNA) has the most updated skills, knowledge, and competence needed in the industry.\"","durationMs":5646,"url":"https://training.linuxfoundation.org/kcna-program-changes/"}}
