{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeLtno27qdPGphrwep3sJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NTBwHUvkYXPZuQFbzGjt6y","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\sources\\lf-mc-exam-faq-2026-08-23.md","content":"---\nsource_url: \"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/faq-mc\"\nfetched_at: \"2026-08-23T23:50:00-0400\"\nauthority: \"The Linux Foundation — official candidate-facing Training & Certification documentation (T&C DOCS), 'Multiple Choice Exams: Frequently Asked Questions'\"\nobjectives_covered: []\nconcepts_covered: [\"kcna-exam-format\", \"published-vs-commonly-reported\"]\n---\n\n# Multiple Choice Exams: Frequently Asked Questions — Linux Foundation T&C DOCS\n\n> **This snapshot changes a load-bearing Chapter 1 claim.** See the research\n> manifest, \"Corrections required before drafting\".\n\nThis is the Linux Foundation's own candidate-facing certification handbook\ndocumentation, not a third-party site. It governs the Linux Foundation's\nmultiple-choice exams as a class. The KCNA exam page describes KCNA as \"an\nonline, proctored, multiple-choice exam\" (see `lf-kcna-exam-page-2026-08-23.md`),\nwhich places KCNA in this class.\n\n## Passing score — PUBLISHED\n\nVerbatim:\n\n> \"A score of 75% or above must be earned to pass the Multiple Choice Exam.\"\n\n## Duration — PUBLISHED\n\nVerbatim:\n\n> \"Candidates are allowed 90 minutes to complete Multiple Choice Exams, with the exception of CNPA. CNPA candidates are allowed 120 minutes to complete the exam.\"\n\n## Question count — NOT PUBLISHED\n\nConfirmed absent on targeted re-fetch 2026-08-23: the FAQ contains **no**\nstatement of how many questions a multiple-choice exam contains, and no\nstatement that the number varies by exam.\n\n## Scoring methodology — NOT PUBLISHED\n\nThe FAQ does not mention scaled scoring, cut scores, or psychometric standard\nsetting. It contains no statement about whether cut scores are published beyond\nthe individual candidate score report.\n\n## Scope caveat for the drafting stage\n\nThe FAQ is titled for multiple-choice exams generally and **does not enumerate\nwhich exams it covers**. CNPA is named as a timing exception; the renewal\nsection references KCNA, KCSA, and CKA/CKAD/CKS in the context of the CARE\nprogram. So:\n\n- The 75% figure is published by the Linux Foundation, for multiple-choice\n  exams as a class.\n- The page does not say \"KCNA: 75%\" in those words.\n\nAccurate phrasings supported by this snapshot:\n\n- ✅ \"The Linux Foundation publishes a 75% passing standard for its\n  multiple-choice exams, of which the KCNA is one.\"\n- ❌ \"The Linux Foundation does not publish a passing score.\" — **false**, do\n  not write this.\n- ❌ \"The KCNA exam page states the passing score is 75%.\" — **false**, it is\n  in the candidate handbook, not on the exam page.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2565,"cache_read_input_tokens":88550,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2565},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6ba44a35-dfac-469b-9317-2d811c689d53","uuid":"9ec183c8-5e56-44bf-bfe2-d29a9e8e1789","timestamp":"2026-08-24T03:51:41.803Z","request_id":"req_011CeLtnmmTwYXY9QpXYMWpm"}
